ity, attention, concern for others. Weaknesses: communication, egocentric, lack of learning. Could be problematic for crew cooperation and adaptability.\n\nCandidate B: very conscientious (reliability), handles stress well (stress resilience), good at assessing weather (technical), excellent computer skills (technical), but regarded as pretentious, sometimes adopts wrong tone (communication). So strengths: reliability, stress, technical. Weakness: communication style.\n\nCandidate C: anticipates dangerous situations, sees complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership, but unfriendly, eats unhealthily. Strengths: technical competence, decision anticipation, leadership. Weakness: unfriendly (crew cooperation), health maybe reliability.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, concentrates very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, but moody, loner. Strengths: problem solving, responsibility, concentration. Weakness: moodiness, loner (crew cooperation).\n\nAll have some concerns. Which is best overall? B seems strong on reliability and stress, but communication issues. A has egocentric and communication difficulty. C has leadership but unfriendly. D has responsibility but moody.\n\nMaybe B is best overall if communication can be coached. Let's propose B as provisional recommendation, citing strengths and acknowledging concerns.\n\nWe should also note that we haven't discussed all candidates yet, but we can start with B. Provide evidence.\n\nThus public message: I recommend Candidate B, because of conscientiousness, stress handling, weather assessment, but note communication concerns. Also ask maybe about crew cooperation evidence from others? But we can just state.\n\nWe need METADATA_JSON with vote.\n\nProceed."}
